# Mindsets

This source documents "Mindsets" as a universal mental model for navigating complex situations through pattern and relationship recognition. It references Carol S. Dweck's research on self-theories and motivation, drawing from *Mindset* and *Self-Theories: Their Role in Motivation, Personality and Development*.

## Key Points

- Mindsets function as a conceptual tool or principle for understanding and navigating complex situations
- They provide a mental shortcut or framework for making sense of patterns and relationships
- Applicable universally across domains
- Confidence level: 0.7 (moderate)
- Referenced sources: Carol S. Dweck's *Mindset* and *Self-Theories*
- Related to [[growth-mindset]], [[mindset---carol-s-dweck]], and [[grit-concept]]

## Cross-Source Perspectives

This mental model connects to Carol S. Dweck's work on self-theories and motivation, as well as her book *Mindset*.
